# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Crystal Spray must let its caster choose Aragorn rather than another permanent.
# Forcing: An Island precedes Aragorn in battlefield order, then white is changed to blue before Ponder.
# AI behavior: The human acts in main phase; the opponent has no relevant choices.
# Failure modes:
#   PASS = the player can target Aragorn and Ponder creates both applicable triggers.
#   FAIL = the engine silently targets the first permanent and Ponder creates only the native blue trigger.
#   TIMEOUT = target or color-word selection does not reach the player.
# Card roles:
#   First Island — distinguishes an explicit target from first-card selection.
#   Aragorn, the Uniter — intended Crystal Spray target.
#   Crystal Spray — changes white to blue until end of turn.
#   Ponder — subsequent monoblue spell.
# Protocol path: target selection, color-word choices, and triggered ability creation.
[metadata]
Name:Explicit text-change targeting
Goal:Survive
Turns:3
Difficulty:Tutorial
Description:Target Aragorn with Crystal Spray, change white to blue, then cast Ponder.

